  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "n910TmmYuSZC1p1vhfHbemlPOTo=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:34:11.901Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The invariant is stated as the heart of the system: *for a given document id `D`, all successful mutations land on the same backend `B(D)` for as long as `D` exists.* Reads may go anywhere, but the MVP routes them with the same function for simplicity and cache affinity.\n\nStandard nginx behaviour is the enemy of that invariant. nginx skips peers marked `down` \u2014 whether by passive `max_fails` tracking or by an active healthcheck calling `set_peer_down` \u2014 and picks the next slot in the ring. Under the pinning invariant that is **catastrophic**: a document pinned to a dead backend would silently re-route to a different instance and split-brain its write log.\n\nSo both paths are disabled, and the disabling is the load-bearing design:\n\n- `upstreams.conf` sets **`max_fails=0`** per `server`, so passive checks never mark a peer down;\n- `lua/healthcheck.lua` runs its own probe loop (every 2 s, 1 s timeout, fall 3 / rise 2, against `GET /health`), tracks state in `lua_shared_dict healthcheck` for `/__hc/status` to render, and **never calls `set_peer_down`**;\n- `proxy_next_upstream off` means no retry across backends;\n- the resulting TCP refusal or timeout is translated to a uniform **503** via `proxy_intercept_errors on; error_page 502 504 = @no_backend;`, with nginx's finer distinction preserved in `$upstream_status` for operators.\n\nNet effect: every peer always looks \"up\" to the upstream module, the hash module always picks the originally-hashed peer, and **the healthcheck's job is observability, not routing**. A dead pin fails closed. The integration test asserts the strict property directly: 5/5 requests pinned to a stopped backend get 503, never a 200 from a different one.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/switchboard-lb/ARCHITECTURE.md` \u2014 \u00a75.1 Invariant; \u00a75.2 Mechanism (pinning under failure); \u00a74.5 Failure modes; \u00a78 M3\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:34:11.901Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:34:11.901Z"
    }
  },
